 Opening the game, loading a save file, then going to main menu, opening sevopedia index and typing a sequence like "xsv" in search bar causes a crash that is reproducible. And does not happen if just opening the game (without loading a save file) and typing such a sequence.
 
 Fixed with the help of Claude code Opus 4.6 thanks in [CvGameInterface.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvGameInterface.cpp).
+
+## 108 - (Fixed) Base AdvCiv diplomacy inconsistency: AI can refuse "tribute" for pure Vassal/Surrender, then accept the same deal through "What do you want in exchange?" with nothing added
+
+Screenshots/files for this issue: [google drive folder link](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1sVkCzmBWbkdVvPDLqog3Hr_2-J6sab0q?usp=sharing).
+
+Repro from diplomacy screen:
+
+- AI offers only `Vassal State` (or `Surrender`) and no extra terms.
+- Clicking `We demand that you give this to us in tribute.` can return refusal (`Not bloody likely`).
+- Clicking `What do you want for this?` right after can return a counter with **nothing extra** and then accept.
+
+So both paths lead to the same final terms, but one refuses first, which is inconsistent and confusing.
+
+Fix:
+
+- In `CvPlayerAI::AI_considerOffer` (file: [CvPlayerAI.cpp](/CvGameCoreDLL/CvPlayerAI.cpp)), add an early human-only acceptance shortcut for the exact one-item pure vassal/surrender shape (one side has only `TRADE_VASSAL` or `TRADE_SURRENDER`, other side empty), before stricter denial/value branches.
+- In `CvDiplomacy.py` (file: [Assets/Python/CvDiplomacy.py](/Assets/Python/CvDiplomacy.py)), when this narrow pure vassal/surrender case is accepted, skip firing generic `DIPLOEVENT_MADE_DEMAND` to avoid regular tribute-demand memory side effects for this specific acceptance path.
+
+Result:
+
+- Tribute/Demand and "What do you want in exchange?" now agree for this case.
+- Player no longer has to do an extra click sequence to get the same no-extra acceptance.

diff --git a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
index de61f48cc..7f4c80a2c 100644
--- a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
+++ b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
@@ -227,6 +227,7 @@ Note 2: Master–vassal(s) changes are intended to strengthen overall AI play by
 - **Master–vassal(s) locus first for tech trades:** Whenever the AI wants to contact other players for a tech trade in `CvPlayerAI::AI_doDiplo`, it now **first checks** whether the desired tech is already tradeable inside its own master–vassal locus (master, vassals, sibling vassals). If so, it **does not ask outside civilizations for that tech**, nudging trades to stay within the group instead. In one autoplay sample this *seemed* to help Ewuare win earlier by finally picking up the Dragoon-related military tech from a vassal, while the locus kept a similar overall tech pace to previous runs. See [KI#79](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#79---improved-before-contacting-other-players-for-tech-trades-first-check-if-we-dont-already-have-the-tech-in-our-master-vassals-locus-and-if-so-dont-contact-the-other-players).
 - **Military priority in tech trades when behind:** When evaluating the value of a tech in trades with players outside the AI’s master–vassal(s) locus in `CvTeamAI::AI_techTradeVal`, the AI values **key military techs** (high `FLAVOR_MILITARY`) more highly if it is **weaker** than its rivals (they matter more for survival than additional economic techs); as of now most such military techs are **untradeable**, which is consistent with autoplay impact being small, but this may matter more if some of them become tradeable.
 - **Devaluation of locus-known techs from outsiders:** When evaluating the value of a tech in trades with players *outside* the AI’s master–vassal(s) locus in `CvTeamAI::AI_techTradeVal`, the AI values techs that any member of its locus already knows **moderately less** when they are offered by outsiders (since that knowledge is already available within the group). In one autoplay sample this *seemed* to contribute to more decisive wins for AIs that had accumulated more vassals.
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5480+) **Tribute/counter-propose consistency fix for pure Vassal/Surrender offers:** base AdvCiv/BtS diplomacy would **reject** direct **Tribute/Demand** ("Not bloody likely"), yet clicking **"What do you want in exchange?"** would **accept** for the same demand (with nothing extra). So players had to do an unnecessary extra click to get the same vassal result. Fixed by making `CvPlayerAI::AI_considerOffer` accept this exact pure one-item vassal/surrender demand directly, and by making [CvDiplomacy.py](/Assets/Python/CvDiplomacy.py) not remember this narrow accepted case as a tribute demand memory (because this is rather a UI consistency fix). See [KI#108](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#108---fixed-base-advciv-diplomacy-inconsistency-ai-can-refuse-tribute-for-pure-vassalsurrender-then-accept-the-same-deal-through-what-do-you-want-in-exchange-with-nothing-added).
 
